 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "How did one king rule four continents from a desk?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "That was Philip the Second of Spain. Spaniards called him the Paper King."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What did he inherit?",
   "scene": "start",
   "date": "16 January 1556",
   "place": "Europe"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "At twenty-eight, his exhausted father handed him Spain, the Netherlands, much of Italy, and the Americas."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Even the Philippines are named after him.",
   "scene": "philippines",
   "date": "",
   "place": "The Philippines",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Was he king of anywhere else?",
   "scene": "mary",
   "date": "1554",
   "place": "England",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "He married four times. One wife was Queen Mary of England, so for four years, he was king of England too."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Why the Paper King?",
   "scene": "escorial",
   "date": "1563 – 1584",
   "place": "El Escorial",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.4,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "He built El Escorial, a palace and monastery in one. From a small office inside, he read every report himself.",
   "scene": "office",
   "date": ""
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Was his family happy?",
   "scene": "carlos",
   "date": "1568",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Not exactly. His son, Don Carlos, grew unstable. Philip had him locked up. Six months later, Carlos was dead."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Enemies said the king had killed his own son. No one has ever proved it."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "At Lepanto in 1571, his fleet helped crush the Ottoman navy. A wounded soldier on board was named Miguel de Cervantes.",
   "scene": "lepanto",
   "date": "7 October 1571",
   "place": "Lepanto",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.4,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.6,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Did his lands keep growing?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "1580",
   "place": "Europe"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Right. In 1580 he took the crown of Portugal, with its own empire. Now the sun truly never set on his lands."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "But it all ran on borrowed silver. And one queen was about to challenge him.",
   "scene": "elizabeth",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.35,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Next time: the Armada. Like the video and follow History Sketches.",
   "scene": "sofonisba",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.35,
     1.2
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And tell us in the comments what you think!"
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "text": "Next: the Armada",
   "sub": "Follow History Sketches"
  }
 ],
